{%- comment -%}
  Fabric and construction — the craft story on the PDP, replacing the nine
  trust badges that sat here.

  Layout follows the iGel feature carousel: heading left, arrow pair opposite
  it on the same line, then a horizontal track of tall cards showing three at a
  time. Each caption is a white box floating inside the bottom of its own
  image, inset from the edges, reading "Label: benefit".

  Colour is JJW's, not the reference's: cream canvas, navy type, white boxes.
  The reference tints its heading light blue on white; ours is navy on cream,
  which is 12.2:1 rather than its ~2.5:1.

  Photography is the JJW _universal set: weave, collar, shoulder seam, hem.
  Shot on undyed cotton, so it shares the cream family with the page — the
  white caption box is what separates the two.

  Every claim has to match snippets/product-accordions.liquid, which already
  says "100% cotton jersey, pre-shrunk and skin-friendly". Nothing here invents
  a number — no GSM, no thread count — because none is established anywhere.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign detail_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'detail'
  assign spec_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'spec'
-%}

{%- style -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} {
    background: var(--cream);
    padding-block: 8rem;
  }

  /* --- Head row: heading left, arrows right ------------------------------ */

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__heading {
    max-width: 20ch;
    letter-spacing: 0.06rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__intro {
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__intro :where(p) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__story {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 4.4rem;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.25rem;
    text-underline-offset: 0.5rem;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__story:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--gold);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrows {
    display: flex;
    flex: none;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Solid navy discs, matching the related-products carousel further down the
    same page — an outlined pair read as a different component sitting on the
    same template.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 5.6rem;
    width: 5.6rem;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--cream);
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: background 0.2s var(--ease), opacity 0.2s var(--ease);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow svg {
    height: 1.8rem;
    width: 2.2rem;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow:hover {
    background: var(--blue);
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Disabled rather than hidden at the ends, as the reference does — the pair
    keeps its position so the head row does not reflow mid-scroll.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.35;
    cursor: default;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow[disabled]:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  /* --- Track ------------------------------------------------------------- */

  {%- comment -%}
    A scroll container, not a transform carousel: swipe works for free on
    touch, the arrows just drive scrollLeft, and with JS off it is still a
    scrollable row rather than a dead frame.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__track {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2.4rem;
    margin: 5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    overflow-x: auto;
    {%- comment -%}
      proximity, not mandatory. Snap points sit at each card's start — 0, 474,
      948 — but with four cards and three in view the track only scrolls 473px
      total. Every point except 0 was out of reach, so mandatory snapped it
      straight back and the arrows moved nothing at all. The same trap waits at
      phone width, where the last card starts past the end of the scroll range.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    scroll-snap-type: x proximity;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    -ms-overflow-style: none;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__track::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Each card carries a brand tint. The photography is all undyed cotton, so
    without it four cream squares sat on a cream canvas and the section read
    as the only colourless band on the page. The tint shows as the frame
    around the inset photo, and again behind the caption.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__card {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 calc((100% - 4.8rem) / 3);
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--tone-bg, var(--blue-bg));
    border-radius: 2.4rem;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} [data-tone='pink'] { --tone-bg: var(--pink-bg); }
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} [data-tone='blue'] { --tone-bg: var(--blue-bg); }
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} [data-tone='gold'] { --tone-bg: var(--gold-bg); }
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} [data-tone='green'] { --tone-bg: var(--green-bg); }
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} [data-tone='purple'] { --tone-bg: var(--purple-bg); }

  /* Gives the end of the track a reachable snap point, since the last card's
     own start lies beyond the maximum scroll offset. */
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__card:last-child {
    scroll-snap-align: end;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    cover, not contain: these are macro textures with no subject to protect,
    so filling the frame reads better than floating them on the card.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__card img {
    height: 100%;
    width: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 1.6rem;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Navy on the card's own tint, not on white. That pairing is 9.9:1 at the
    lightest tint we use, where tinting the type instead would have failed —
    Heart Pink on white is 3.1:1 and Sunshine Gold 2.1:1. Same rule the
    collection card titles follow: the colour lives in the fill.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__caption {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 2.4rem;
    bottom: 2.4rem;
    /* A <p> keeps its 1em margin even when absolutely positioned, which pushed
       the box 17px above the 2.4rem inset and broke the even frame. */
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.8rem 2rem;
    background: var(--tone-bg, var(--blue-bg));
    border-radius: 1.6rem;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__caption strong {
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* --- Spec strip -------------------------------------------------------- */

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__specs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat({{ spec_blocks.size | at_least: 1 }}, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin: 4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--white);
    border-radius: 2rem;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec {
    padding: 2.4rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec + .fs__spec {
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--sky);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec dt {
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: 0.12rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec dd {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__track {
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrow {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 989px) {
    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__card {
      flex-basis: calc((100% - 2.4rem) / 2);
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__specs {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      Wrapping to two rows makes the inline dividers land in the wrong place —
      the third cell would keep a left border while starting a row. Reset, then
      draw the rules the two-column shape actually needs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec + .fs__spec {
      border-inline-start: 0;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec:nth-child(even) {
      border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--sky);
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec:nth-child(n + 3) {
      border-block-start: 2px solid var(--sky);
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} {
      padding-block: 5rem;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__heading {
      max-width: none;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__intro {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      Arrows go at phone width — the track is swiped, and a 5.6rem pair beside
      a 4rem heading crowds the row. The peeking second card is the affordance.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__arrows {
      display: none;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__track {
      gap: 1.6rem;
      margin-top: 3.2rem;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__card {
      flex-basis: 84%;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__caption {
      inset-inline: 1.6rem;
      bottom: 1.6rem;
      padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec {
      padding: 1.8rem 1.2rem;
    }

    #FabricStory-{{ section.id }} .fs__spec dd {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section id="FabricStory-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="page-width">
    <div class="fs__head">
      <div>
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="hxxl fs__heading scroll-trigger animate--fade-in">
            {{- section.settings.heading | escape -}}
          </h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
          <div class="fs__intro scroll-trigger animate--fade-in">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} Shown only once a page with this handle exists, so it never 404s. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign story_page = blank
          if section.settings.story_handle != blank and section.settings.story_label != blank
            assign story_page = pages[section.settings.story_handle]
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if story_page.id != blank -%}
          <a class="fs__story" href="{{ story_page.url }}">{{ section.settings.story_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if detail_blocks.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="fs__arrows">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="fs__arrow"
            data-fs-prev
            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.previous' | t }}"
            aria-controls="FabricTrack-{{ section.id }}"
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path fill="currentColor" d="M7.21.15a.5.5 0 0 1 .7.71L3.77 6H19.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H3.77l4.14 5.14a.5.5 0 0 1-.78.62l-4.9-6.08a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.63z"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="fs__arrow"
            data-fs-next
            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.next' | t }}"
            aria-controls="FabricTrack-{{ section.id }}"
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path fill="currentColor" d="M12.79.15a.5.5 0 0 0-.7.71L16.23 6H.5a.5.5 0 0 0 0 1h15.73l-4.14 5.14a.5.5 0 0 0 .78.62l4.9-6.08a.5.5 0 0 0 0-.63z"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if detail_blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="fs__track" id="FabricTrack-{{ section.id }}" tabindex="0">
        {%- for block in detail_blocks -%}
          <li class="fs__card" data-tone="{{ block.settings.tone }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- comment -%}
              Merchant upload wins; otherwise one of the four photos that ship
              with the theme. The select means a card can never point at an
              asset that is not there, so this degrades to no media rather
              than to a broken <img>.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
              {{
                block.settings.image
                | image_url: width: 900
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  alt: block.settings.title,
                  widths: '400, 650, 900',
                  sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 84vw, (max-width: 989px) 46vw, 30vw'
              }}
            {%- elsif block.settings.photo != blank -%}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.photo | asset_img_url: '900x' }}"
                srcset="
                  {{ block.settings.photo | asset_img_url: '400x' }} 400w,
                  {{ block.settings.photo | asset_img_url: '650x' }} 650w,
                  {{ block.settings.photo | asset_img_url: '900x' }} 900w
                "
                sizes="(max-width: 749px) 84vw, (max-width: 989px) 46vw, 30vw"
                alt="{{ block.settings.title | escape }}"
                width="1000"
                height="1000"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if block.settings.title != blank or block.settings.text != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The space before {% endif %} is load-bearing — it is the gap
                after the colon. A dash on that tag would strip it and the
                caption would read "jersey:knitted".
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <p class="fs__caption">
                {%- if block.settings.title != blank %}<strong>{{ block.settings.title | escape }}:</strong> {% endif -%}
                {{- block.settings.text | escape -}}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if spec_blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <dl class="fs__specs scroll-trigger animate--fade-in">
        {%- for block in spec_blocks -%}
          <div class="fs__spec" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <dt>{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</dt>
            <dd>{{ block.settings.value | escape }}</dd>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </dl>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('FabricStory-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root || root.dataset.fsInit) return;
    root.dataset.fsInit = '1';

    var track = root.querySelector('.fs__track');
    var prev = root.querySelector('[data-fs-prev]');
    var next = root.querySelector('[data-fs-next]');
    if (!track || !prev || !next) return;

    function step() {
      var card = track.querySelector('.fs__card');
      if (!card) return track.clientWidth;
      // One card plus the gap, read from layout rather than hardcoded, so the
      // breakpoints stay the single source of how many are in view.
      var gap = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(track).columnGap) || 0;
      return card.getBoundingClientRect().width + gap;
    }

    function sync() {
      // 1px of slack: fractional widths mean scrollLeft rarely lands exactly.
      var max = track.scrollWidth - track.clientWidth;
      prev.disabled = track.scrollLeft <= 1;
      next.disabled = track.scrollLeft >= max - 1;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      sync() hung entirely off the scroll event, so a single missed event left
      a button disabled — and a disabled button swallows the next click, which
      strands the track at one end for good. The timer re-reads the real
      scrollLeft after the move regardless of what fired.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    var pending;
    function move(direction) {
      // No explicit behavior: an options-object 'smooth' overrides the
      // element's scroll-behavior and would ignore the reduced-motion rule.
      track.scrollBy({ left: direction * step() });
      clearTimeout(pending);
      pending = setTimeout(sync, 450);
    }

    prev.addEventListener('click', function () {
      move(-1);
    });

    next.addEventListener('click', function () {
      move(1);
    });

    track.addEventListener('scroll', sync, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', sync);
    sync();
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Fabric story",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Made to Survive Recess"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "<p>The details that decide whether a tee lasts one term or three</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "story_label",
      "label": "Story link label",
      "default": "See how it's made"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "story_handle",
      "label": "Story page handle",
      "info": "The link shows only once a page with this handle exists in Online Store > Pages.",
      "default": "how-its-made"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "name": "Detail",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Photo",
          "info": "Overrides the built-in photo below."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "photo",
          "label": "Built-in photo",
          "options": [
            { "value": "", "label": "None" },
            { "value": "jjw-fabric-weave.jpg", "label": "Fabric weave" },
            { "value": "jjw-fabric-collar.jpg", "label": "Collar stretch" },
            { "value": "jjw-fabric-shoulder.jpg", "label": "Shoulder seam" },
            { "value": "jjw-fabric-hem.jpg", "label": "Sleeve hem" }
          ],
          "default": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Label",
          "info": "Shown bold, followed by a colon."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "tone",
          "label": "Card colour",
          "options": [
            { "value": "pink", "label": "Heart Pink" },
            { "value": "blue", "label": "Adventure Blue" },
            { "value": "gold", "label": "Sunshine Gold" },
            { "value": "green", "label": "Outdoor Green" },
            { "value": "purple", "label": "Space Purple" }
          ],
          "default": "blue"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spec",
      "name": "Spec",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Value"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Fabric story"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
